From ef88e4d9f6e626b3cde3630652c0d426038e5b7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 11:32:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 562/572] fix(st): bound check image ID in
 plat_get_image_source
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The generic partition driver falls back to load_backup_gpt with
BKUP_GPT_IMAGE_ID (29) when the primary GPT is corrupted. That ID is
larger than MAX_NUMBER_IDS on the STM32MP platforms, so the policies
array was indexed out of bounds. The existing FCONF getter only
protects that access with an assert, which is compiled out in release
builds.

Reject any image ID beyond the platform policy table so unsupported
images fail cleanly instead of reading past the array.

Coverity issue: CID 1209568: Out-of-bounds access in load_partition_table

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git a7e773d8d27b5b6709b71f4b49223f937f95d601 fix(st): bound check image ID in plat_get_image_source]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Change-Id: If678bc91a634bec4dc725e12a43e3a557a7ea264
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/597393
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 plat/st/common/bl2_io_storage.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/st/common/bl2_io_storage.c b/plat/st/common/bl2_io_storage.c
index cb5ccf5a5c..ae13edc5e6 100644
--- a/plat/st/common/bl2_io_storage.c
+++ b/plat/st/common/bl2_io_storage.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <assert.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
 #include <arch_helpers.h>
@@ -767,6 +768,11 @@ int plat_get_image_source(unsigned int image_id, uintptr_t *dev_handle,
 	int rc;
 	const struct plat_io_policy *policy;
 
+	/* Generic code may request IDs absent from the policy table, e.g. BKUP_GPT_IMAGE_ID */
+	if (image_id >= MAX_NUMBER_IDS) {
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	policy = FCONF_GET_PROPERTY(stm32mp, io_policies, image_id);
 	rc = policy->check(policy->image_spec);
 	if (rc == 0) {
-- 
